From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:49:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hatch_build: accept riscv64 ELF binaries

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: upstream's wheels.yml builds no riscv64 wheel, so the change is not exercised by its own CI]

_verify_elf() maps the ELF e_machine of the built dispatcher to the
arch suffix of the wheel's platform tag and refuses the build when the
machine is unknown. Only x86_64 (62) and aarch64 (183) are listed, so a
riscv64 build fails with "is an ELF for an unsupported machine, which
does not match the linux_riscv64 wheel tag" after cargo has already
produced a working riscv64 binary.

Add EM_RISCV (243). The check stays as strict: riscv64 ELF headers are
little-endian, and the binary must still match the wheel tag.
---
 hatch_build.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hatch_build.py b/hatch_build.py
index e412bcd..d630035 100644
--- a/hatch_build.py
+++ b/hatch_build.py
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ MACOS_TARGETS = ["aarch64-apple-darwin", "x86_64-apple-darwin"]
 MACOS_ARCHS = {"arm64", "x86_64"}
 
 # ELF `e_machine` values, as they are spelled in a wheel platform tag.
-ELF_MACHINES = {62: "x86_64", 183: "aarch64"}
+ELF_MACHINES = {62: "x86_64", 183: "aarch64", 243: "riscv64"}
 
 
 class WrongBinaryError(Exception):
